Subject: Constructors and apply on the record path

What this does
  Constructors and apply on the record path.

Why we need it
  `new` on plain JS constructors and `f.apply(this, arguments)` were the last call shapes that dropped out of the record path into `JS_Call`/`JS_CallInternal`.

What it adds
  `regvm_t_construct_record` (fresh `this` via `js_create_from_ctor_cap`, two extra owned slots for `this`/`new_target`, `JS_CALL_FLAG_CONSTRUCTOR`, return-value selection in `regvm_t_return_nested`); `regvm_t_apply_arguments_record` (callee record with `this` from the operand, args borrowed from the caller's window); both `noinline` and gate frame-exempt.

Needs a bytecode version bump
  No.
